Durable records do not prevent duplicate actors from doing the same work. Every start, retry, watcher fire, transport action, and merge attempt SHOULD be protected by a lease.

## 1. Lease lifecycle

```text
lease.acquire.v1
  -> lease.heartbeat.v1
  -> lease.release.v1 | lease.expire.v1 | lease.revoke.v1
```

A lease names:

- resource id;
- run id;
- owning actor;
- parent actor;
- authority scope;
- idempotency key;
- acquiredAt;
- expiresAt;
- heartbeat interval.

