The long-term direction is to turn the policy into a small executable protocol system rather than a larger prose manual.

## 1. Global to local

A global protocol describes the full conversation among rootActor, parentActor, childActor, delegatedParentActor, transportOnlyActor, reviewer, and merge executor. A local protocol is the subset projected to one actor.

The local protocol SHOULD define:

- messages the actor may send;
- messages the actor may receive;
- required prior state;
- allowed next state;
- required context packet fields;
- forbidden actions;
- completion and escalation exits.

