Canonical state is derived only from append-only records that satisfy all of these conditions:

- the record is schema-valid;
- the record has a stable `eventId`;
- the record has an `eventKind` or `kind` that is in the active protocol;
- the record names the writing actor and actor role;
- the record carries an `idempotencyKey` when it can cause work to start, retry, approve, merge, or transport;
- the record declares causal references to the command, claim, lease, trigger, evidence, or approval it depends on;
- the writer has authority under `.agents/authority-write-gate.md`.

