{"eventId":"evt-000448","eventKind":"doc_section.upsert.v1","status":"accepted","decidedAt":"2026-05-14T00:00:00+09:00","artifactPath":".agents/trigger-engine.md","sectionOrder":3,"sectionId":".agents-trigger-engine.md::0003::3.-Watcher-constraints","headingDepth":2,"headingText":"3. Watcher constraints","headingPath":["Trigger Engine and Join Patterns","3. Watcher constraints"],"content":"## 3. Watcher constraints

A watcher / scheduler / dispatcher MUST NOT infer semantic approval. It may:

- match events;
- acquire lease;
- enqueue command;
- append trigger-fired evidence;
- retry transport;
- notify parent or root.

It MUST NOT:

- approve completion;
- create command outside its authority;
